# .cursorrules — Collections Dialogue Engine
# Read docs/BUILD_SPEC.md first. These rules are non-negotiable and override convenience.

## PROJECT
- A text-in -> text-out engine for RBI-compliant outbound EMI collections.
- Boundary: starts at the ASR transcript, ends at the reply string for TTS.
- DO NOT build or call ASR, TTS, noise-cancellation, turn-detection, or telephony — they are external (Fonada).
- Stack: Python 3.11+, FastAPI, Pydantic v2, Gemini via Vertex AI, Upstash Redis (state/memory),
  external KB endpoint (flows), external tool endpoint (LMS/payment). Async httpx for all external calls.

## THE CORE PRINCIPLE (never violate)
- The LLM UNDERSTANDS; deterministic code DECIDES; the compliance gate has the FINAL word.
- The LLM (Gemini) emits ONLY structured commands (start_flow/set_slot/cancel_flow/clarify/human_handoff/cannot_handle).
- The LLM NEVER writes the final reply text and NEVER decides policy or how hard to press.
- NEVER put business rules or compliance rules inside any LLM prompt. They live in code/flows only.
- Treat all LLM output as untrusted: parse, validate against the Command vocabulary, reject anything else.

## DECISIONS & COMPLIANCE (hard constraints)
- The compliance gate (engine/gate.py) runs on EVERY outbound line and may block/substitute. Nothing bypasses it.
- Order: safety pre-empt -> dispute/fraud -> contact-limit/opt-out gates run BEFORE any recovery logic.
- The bot may be firm but NEVER threatens, shames, abuses, uses false urgency, or discloses debt to third parties.
- Contact only within configured call-window hours; honor opt-outs, dispute holds, attempt caps, vulnerable flags.
- On distress/vulnerability/crisis: suspend recovery, route to a human, suppress dunning. High recall preferred.
- Human-owned actions (settlement, restructuring, legal-prep, vulnerable handling) are NEVER auto-executed.
- Trust/persona/risk scores are INPUTS, never licenses — they never authorize gate-prohibited conduct.

## TOOLS
- WRITE tools (create_payment_link, raise_dispute_ticket, schedule_followup, log_disposition) are called
  ONLY by the executor as defined flow steps, with an idempotency_key. NEVER at LLM discretion.
- READ tools (check_last_payment, get_balance, get_borrower) may be called by executor steps; cache within a turn.
- All tool calls go through clients/tools.py to the external tool endpoint. Handle timeouts; degrade to human-handoff on failure, never crash a turn.

## STATE, MEMORY & AUDIT
- Live call state in Upstash key state:{call_id} (TTL). Durable borrower memory in borrower:{borrower_id} (14 blocks).
- Load state + hydrate from borrower record at turn start; save both at turn end. Use the version field for optimistic concurrency.
- Every turn appends an immutable audit record reconstructing: intent/commands -> decision -> tools -> gate verdict -> reply.
- NEVER write PII (phone/account numbers) to logs — mask it. Audit lives in the store, not in plaintext logs.

## BUILD DISCIPLINE
- Build sprint-by-sprint in the order in BUILD_SPEC.md. Do not start a sprint until the prior DoD is green.
- Sprint 2 (executor) is built and tested with HARDCODED commands and NO LLM. Prove the deterministic core first.
- From Sprint 6 on, the compliance suite (tests/compliance/) is the release gate: never merge it red.
- Validate flow YAML at load (every branch target exists; no progress-free loops). Never use eval() for conditions.
- Keep <= 1 LLM call per turn on the live path (latency). Keep persona/emotion classifiers off the hot path or cached.
- Anything uncertain about external contracts: leave a `# DECISION NEEDED:` comment and use the documented default.

## STYLE
- Pydantic v2 models for every boundary (API, command, state, flow, tool I/O). Full type hints; mypy clean.
- ruff + black clean. Async everywhere for I/O. Small, testable, single-responsibility modules per the repo layout.
- Templated responses only (no free-form LLM generation of borrower-facing text). Spoken-form + language from config.
